# pnpm owns this file. Seed S-028 added `pnpm format:check` to the web CI job on
# 2026-08-22, and there was no .prettierignore, so the sweep reformatted
# pnpm-lock.yaml as well: 4244 insertions, 1493 deletions, YAML flow mappings
# rewritten as block mappings.
#
# That put two tools in charge of one file. Measured on the batch-13 integration
# tree, 2026-08-22: `pnpm install --lockfile-only` rewrites the lockfile back to
# pnpm's own style, reversing the prettier diff exactly, and `pnpm format:check`
# then exits 1 with "[warn] pnpm-lock.yaml". So the next `pnpm add` would have
# broken CI, and the fix would have been to run prettier over a file pnpm
# regenerates. Ignoring it hands the file back to the tool that writes it.
pnpm-lock.yaml

